---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AREAS } from "../../data/areas";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Areas", path: "/areas" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Areas covered"
  description="Devine Plumbing and Heating says it is local to Bedfordshire. The Google pin is near Edenham, Lincolnshire. Towns, and how to check your street. Call 07436 135412."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="wrap page-hero prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Areas</p>
    <h1>Areas</h1>
    <p>
      Two facts, both from the Google profile. The description says the firm is local to
      Bedfordshire. The pin is near Edenham, South Kesteven, Lincolnshire, a few miles from Bourne.
      There is no list of towns on the profile, and no shop address.
    </p>
    <p>
      The pages below are the main towns in that county and around that pin. They are here so you
      can check the sort of houses and water you have, then call. They are not a promise that every
      street is inside a fixed radius.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0.5rem">
    <div class="wrap area-grid">
      {
        AREAS.map((area) => (
          <article class="area-card">
            <p class="muted">{area.county}</p>
            <h2 style="font-size:1.8rem">{area.name}</h2>
            <p>{area.paragraphs[0]}</p>
            <p>
              <a href={`/areas/${area.slug}`}>Plumber in {area.name}</a>
            </p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
